Here's the full picture of what the platform exposes — all reachable from n8n via POST http://phoenix:8000/api/... HTTP Request nodes.

Base URL
All requests go through Kong: http://phoenix:8000/api

What n8n can call
1. Workflow Governance (/api/workflow-governance)
The richest surface — purpose-built for n8n workflows.

Endpoint	Method	What it does
/workflows	GET	List all governed workflows (filter by project, tag)
/workflows/:id/score	POST	Compute risk score for a workflow
/workflows/:id/policies/apply	POST	Bind active policies to a workflow
/workflows/:id/applied-policies	GET	See which policies are currently applied
/workflows/:id/analyze	POST	Trigger async AI governance analysis → returns job_id
/workflows/analysis/:job_id	GET	Poll analysis status (pending / completed / failed)
/workflows/analyze/callback/:job_id	POST	n8n calls this to deliver AI analysis results
/workflows/:id/analyses	GET	Full analysis history for a workflow
/workflows/discover	POST	Pull workflow list from a connected platform
/workflows/import	POST	Import a specific workflow from a platform
/risk/summary	GET	Aggregate risk scores across all workflows
/risk/pii/:pii_type	GET	Which workflows expose a given PII type
/risk/nodes	GET	Node-level risk aggregates
/tags	GET/POST/PUT/DELETE	Tag registry CRUD
/platforms	GET/POST/PUT/DELETE	Platform connection registry (n8n, Make, Zapier, Camunda)
/platforms/:id/test	POST	Test live connectivity to a registered platform
Key automation pattern: n8n is both the consumer and producer here. The platform calls n8n to run AI analysis, and n8n calls the callback endpoint to return results.

2. Policy Engine (/api/governance)
Endpoint	Method	What it does
/policies	GET	List policies (filter by status, workflow_id)
/policies/:id	GET	Policy detail with rules, bindings, violation counts
/policies	POST	Create a policy
/policies/:id/status	PATCH	Activate or deactivate
/policies/:id/rules	POST/DELETE	Add or remove rules
/policies/:id/bindings	GET/POST/DELETE	Bind/unbind policy to targets
/violations	GET	List violations (filter by workflow_id, policy_id, status, severity)
/violations/evaluate	POST	Run policy evaluation against workflow_id → creates violations
/violations/summary	GET	Violation counts grouped by workflow
/violations/:id/status	PATCH	Acknowledge / resolve / close a violation
/rule-schemas	GET	List all available rule types
/rule-schemas/:type	GET	JSON schema for a specific rule type
3. Escalation (/api/escalation)
Endpoint	Method	What it does
/incidents	GET	List incidents (filter by status, severity)
/incidents	POST	Trigger an incident (title, severity, context_json)
/incidents/:id	GET	Incident detail with notification log
/incidents/:id/status	PATCH	Transition state: open → acknowledged → resolved → closed
/incidents/:id/log	POST	Append a notification log entry
/rules	GET/POST/PUT/DELETE	Escalation rule CRUD
4. Audit Log (/api/audit)
Endpoint	Method	What it does
/events	POST	Append a compliance event (append-only)
/events	GET	Query audit events (range-scoped, partitioned by month)
/events/summary	GET	Aggregate counts
5. AI Inference (/api/inference)
Endpoint	Method	What it does
/models	GET/POST/PUT/DELETE	Model registry CRUD
/inference	GET/POST	List or submit inference requests
/inference/:id	GET	Request detail with decisions
/inference/:id/decisions	POST	Record a governance decision against a request
/inference/decisions	GET	Cross-request decision list (filter by policy_id, outcome)
/inference/:id/status	PATCH	Update request status
6. Telemetry (/api/telemetry)
Endpoint	Method	What it does
/metrics	POST	Ingest a metric data point
/metrics	GET	Query metrics (time-range scoped, TimescaleDB backed)
High-value n8n workflow patterns
Governance enforcement pipeline


Schedule/Webhook → GET /workflow-governance/workflows
→ POST /workflow-governance/workflows/:id/score
→ [if score > threshold] POST /governance/violations/evaluate
→ [if violations] POST /escalation/incidents
→ POST /audit/events
Scheduled compliance sweep


Cron → GET /governance/violations?status=open&severity=critical
→ [for each] PATCH /governance/violations/:id/status (acknowledge)
→ POST /escalation/incidents (if new critical ones)
→ Slack/email notification
New workflow auto-govern on import


Webhook (n8n workflow published) → POST /workflow-governance/workflows/import
→ POST /workflow-governance/workflows/:id/score
→ POST /workflow-governance/workflows/:id/policies/apply
→ POST /workflow-governance/workflows/:id/analyze  (triggers AI analysis back to n8n)
Incident response automation


Webhook on POST /escalation/incidents
→ route by severity (IF node)
→ critical: page on-call + POST /audit/events
→ high: Slack + PATCH /incidents/:id/status = acknowledged